0.  THE PREDICTED NORMALISATION -- and a factor 2 pi in the proposal that has to be corrected first
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    canonical  a_0 = 9.360e-11 m/s^2 :  a_0/G = 1.4025 kg/m^2 =    671.4 Msun/pc^2 |  a_0/(2 pi G) =  106.9 Msun/pc^2
    alt        a_0 = 1.130e-10 m/s^2 :  a_0/G = 1.6931 kg/m^2 =    810.5 Msun/pc^2 |  a_0/(2 pi G) =  129.0 Msun/pc^2
  [PASS] P1.0 THE PROPOSAL'S PREDICTED NORMALISATION IS WRONG BY 2 pi, and the correction is verified here: the numbers 107 / 129 Msun/pc^2 that P1 calls 'a_0/G' are a_0/(2 pi G), the item-5 halo surface-density constant itself. The vertical unit of the collapse is a_0/G = 671 / 811 Msun/pc^2   (a_0/G = 671.4 / 810.5; a_0/(2 pi G) = 106.9 / 129.0; ratio to the quoted 107 is 6.2745 = 2 pi)

