    canonical : released g_bar spans 1.382e-15 .. 3.917e-12 m/s^2  ->  y = g_bar/a_0 in [1.48e-05, 0.042],  S in [4.89, 260.2]
                 largest departure of f(S) from its deep-MOND asymptote anywhere in the data: +13.55%  (at y = 0.042)
    alt       : released g_bar spans 1.382e-15 .. 3.917e-12 m/s^2  ->  y = g_bar/a_0 in [1.22e-05, 0.035],  S in [5.37, 285.9]
                 largest departure of f(S) from its deep-MOND asymptote anywhere in the data: +12.29%  (at y = 0.035)
  [PASS] P1.2a AGAINST THE PROPOSAL: the released KiDS lensing RAR never reaches the regime P1 named. P1 said its non-restatement content is the collapse THROUGH the transition, at S <~ 3; the innermost point of the deepest stack sits at S = 4.9, and 14 of the 15 acceleration bins are at S > 8   (S_min over all 16 stacks = 4.89 (y_max = 0.0418); P1 asked for S <~ 3. The largest kernel-over-deep-MOND correction anywhere in the data is 13.5%, at that one bin)

    full Route A kernel, a_0 free : a_0 = 1.852e-10  chi2_min =   125.71  on 60 points
    bare deep MOND  v^4=GM a_0    : a_0 = 1.962e-10  chi2_min =   114.21
  [PASS] P1.2b THE RESTATEMENT TEST IN ITS DECISIVE FORM, and it says RESTATEMENT for every purpose P1 claims: the a_0 these data return is the same to 0.03 dex whether it is read through the full Route A kernel or through the bare deep-MOND algebra v^4 = G M_b a_0. Nothing P1 measures is separable from the deep-MOND law. IS_RESTATEMENT = TRUE   (a_0(full kernel) = 1.852e-10, a_0(bare deep MOND) = 1.962e-10: 0.025 dex apart, against a 0.082 dex footing separation and a 0.05 dex second-law target)
    delta chi2 (deep - full)      = -11.50 on 60 points at equal parameter count (-5.40 after inflating errors to chi2/dof = 1)
    same, dropping the 3 innermost (highest g_bar) bins = -0.86 on 48 points
  [PASS] P1.2c AGAINST INTEREST: the one place the kernel's transition is visible in these data, it points the wrong way. With the same number of free parameters the BARE deep-MOND asymptote fits better than the full Route A kernel, and the preference lives entirely in the three innermost acceleration bins -- exactly where miscentring and the lens's own baryonic extent live (h113 flagged the same radii). Reported, not banked either way   (deep favoured by 11.5 on all 60 points (5.4 inflated), but only 0.9 once the 3 innermost bins are dropped)

